This is the travel and skill-capping adaptation of the meta Pious Renewal bar. Pious Assault supplies the repeatable teardown, while Twin Moon Sweep supplies an unblockable double strike and self-heal. Aura of Holy Might remains a core part of the damage engine rather than an optional skill. Mirage Cloak adds blocking and nearby earth damage whenever a Dervish enchantment is removed; the linked meta bar's 6+1 Earth Prayers investment is retained for it. An of-enchanting scythe extends Mirage Cloak's 20-second duration to match its 24-second recharge when it is not removed.

Pious Haste is the default travel choice because its 50% removal-effect speed boost remains useful while leading the heroes, moving outside shout range, or crossing traps. Use Pious Haste between groups and Pious Fury after stopping to fight. Both are stances, so activating either one ends the other.

<pvxbig>
[[image:Optional.jpg|25px]] '''Optional Damage Skills (when relying on hero speed)''' :
*{{skill pvxicon|Irresistible Sweep|16}} over Pious Haste for the best general-purpose third attack: reliable bonus damage, an unblockable removal effect, and stance removal.
*{{skill pvxicon|Wearying Strike|16}} over Pious Haste for Deep Wound against bosses and other high-Health targets; it is less useful against short-lived Normal Mode groups.

[[image:Optional.jpg|25px]] '''Optional Buff/Utility Skills''' :
*{{skill pvxicon|Death's Charge|3}} over Pious Haste after changing to D/A, for a shadow step and conditional heal when hero shouts already cover travel. It can place the player ahead of hero support; use it at 0 Shadow Arts, or reduce base Earth Prayers to 5 for 3 Shadow Arts and a stronger heal.
*{{skill pvxicon|"I Am Unstoppable!"|5}} over Twin Moon Sweep for knock-down and Cripple protection on hazardous skill-capture routes, or over Signet of Capture when no elite is needed.
*{{skill pvxicon|Fleeting Stability|7}} over Pious Haste for more frequent knock-down protection and a maintainable 25% speed boost. Cast it before Pious Renewal so the next teardown removes Renewal instead.
*{{skill pvxicon|Signet of Capture}} over Twin Moon Sweep as a second copy when the route contains two desired elites; Pious Assault can operate the teardown engine alone.
