When a hero uses a superior main-attribute rune, it belongs on the head armor: hero headgear adds an extra +1 to the attribute of the rune placed there. The other rune locations are interchangeable. Secondary-profession attributes cannot be raised with runes, so the listed Motivation, Command, Channeling Magic, Restoration Magic, Protection Prayers, and Inspiration Magic values are base ranks where those attributes belong to the secondary profession.

==Usage==

===Hero Behavior===
* Set every hero to Avoid Combat while running.
* For a boss fight, change Blinding Air, Invoke Air, Thunderclap Air, and Smiting Channel Support to Guard. Call or attack the boss, then return those four heroes to Avoid Combat when moving on.
* Leave Running Support, Word of Healing, and UA Heal-Prot on Avoid Combat. Their bars contain ally-, party-, or self-targeted skills that remain functional in that mode.
* Avoid Combat heroes generally do not activate skills that directly target foes. This is why Power Drain is not used on either backline Monk.

===Running===
* Incoming! and Fall Back! provide the party's baseline movement speed. Pious Haste gives the player faster independent movement when leading, leaving earshot, or crossing a dangerous gap in the shout cycle.
* Use Pious Haste while traveling and switch to Pious Fury only after stopping to fight; because both are stances, they cannot run simultaneously.
* The movement package also supplies passive or mobile recovery, allowing the team to cross routine Normal Mode areas without stopping to recast a conventional healing engine.

===Combat===
* Engage with the Dervish and let melee enemies gather around the player. Splinter Weapon and Ancestors' Rage convert that natural ball into armor-ignoring and area damage.
* Strength of Honor is maintained on the scythe wielder. Ray of Judgment adds area pressure when enemies remain balled.
* Maintain Aura of Holy Might and Mirage Cloak in combat. Cast Pious Renewal before Pious Fury and before each teardown attack; removing Pious Renewal triggers both damage enchantments while refunding energy and Health.
* Thunderclap supplies nearby Cracked Armor and Weakness. Shock Arrow then becomes an energy-positive attack for Elementalists hitting affected foes.
* Aegis is the primary party-wide attack defense. Blinding Surge and Thunderclap supplement it with Blind and Weakness; Protective Spirit and Shield of Absorption catch focused damage.
* Unyielding Aura is maintained automatically and dismissed by the hero when a party member dies in range, providing low-micro recovery. Signet of Return gives the Running Support hero a second reusable resurrection.

===Skill Capture===
* Check the destination area for capturable elites before leaving the outpost. When two desired elites are present, use the second-Signet option described under the player build.
* The combat core continues to function with Twin Moon Sweep removed, but avoid replacing Pious Renewal, Pious Assault, Pious Fury, Mirage Cloak, or Aura of Holy Might.

===Party-Size Scaling===
* '''Four members:''' Player, Running Support, Word of Healing, and Thunderclap Air.
* '''Six members:''' add UA Heal-Prot and Invoke Air.
* '''Eight members:''' add Blinding Air and Smiting Channel Support.

==Counters==
* Heavy enchantment removal disrupts Pious Renewal, the Elementalist attunements, Strength of Honor, Unyielding Aura, and Aegis.
* Caster-heavy bosses remain the team's largest combat weakness because the roster has no dedicated Domination shutdown or broad spell interruption.
* Daze and energy denial can suppress the caster-heavy team, although Signet of Recall, Glyph of Lesser Energy, Elementalist attunements, and Shock Arrow reduce ordinary energy pressure.
* Knock downs and Cripple can break running formation. Use "I Am Unstoppable!", Fleeting Stability, Aura of Stability, or the Charge! team change described beneath the relevant build when those effects are frequent.
* Mobile or widely scattered enemies reduce the value of Ray of Judgment, Splinter Weapon, and Ancestors' Rage.

==Notes==
* The composition is designed for low-micro Normal Mode travel and short skill-capture fights. It deliberately favors movement, passive recovery, and forgiving hero behavior over the shutdown and energy support of general Hard Mode meta teams.
* The three Air roles share one Cracked Armor engine rather than duplicating Shell Shock. Blinding Surge, Thunderclap, Aegis, and the protection skills layer several forms of physical mitigation without requiring an ST Ritualist.
* Unyielding Aura supplies automatic recovery from deaths and Signet of Return supplies a reusable backup, so additional resurrection slots usually contribute less than damage or route utility.
* See [[gww:Hero behavior|Hero behavior]] and the [[Guide:PvE Equipment|PvE Equipment guide]] for additional mechanics and gearing information.